						"description": "Validates a user session using JWT token provided in request body. **Channel authentication required** - this endpoint only works when accessed via `/channel/accounts/session/validate` URL path with Channel JWT token in Authorization header.\n\n**Authentication:**\n- Requires Channel JWT token (Bearer token) in Authorization header\n- User session JWT token in request body (`jwtToken` field)\n\n**Account Context Resolution:**\n- If `account_id` is in channel JWT → uses it directly\n- If `account_id` is NOT in channel JWT → extracts domain from Host header and looks up account\n- For domain lookup, include Host header: `Host: <domain>` (e.g., `Host: testcompany`)\n\n**User Context Resolution:**\n- If `user_id` is in channel JWT → uses it directly\n- If `user_id` is NOT in channel JWT → extracts `userId` from the user JWT token in request body\n\n**Note:** The URL must contain `/channel/` in the path. Accessing via `/accounts/session/validate` will be rejected."
